# VS BOUTIQUE - PRODUCT ARCHITECTURE & ROADMAP

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW
A premium boutique management and discovery platform (Zomato/Swiggy model) for the fashion industry.

---

## 2. APP STRUCTURE

### A. CUSTOMER MOBILE APP (React Native / Expo)
*   **Discovery**: Location-based boutique search and category filtering.
*   **Gallery**: Full design showcase with price and availability.
*   **Measurement Book**: Digital storage for user body measurements.
*   **Ordering**: Secure checkout, real-time status tracking, and history.
*   **Social**: Ratings, reviews, and wishlist.

### B. OWNER DASHBOARD (React)
*   **Live Simulator**: Real-time preview of boutique profile for the app.
*   **Design Gallery**: CRUD operations for design items.
*   **Service Management**: Specialty and specialty icon mapping.
*   **Order Manager**: Status updates (Received -> Processing -> Ready).
*   **Analytics**: Revenue tracking and client statistics.

### C. SUPER ADMIN PORTAL (React)
*   **Boutique Onboarding**: Approval and verification of new vendors.
*   **User Management**: Managing permissions for owners and admins.
*   **Global Settings**: Category management, pricing rules, and platform fees.
*   **Audit Logs**: Security tracking of all system actions.

---

## 3. PERFECT APP PARAMETERS

### Technical Stack
*   **Frontend**: React (Web), React Native (Mobile).
*   **Backend**: Node.js, Express.
*   **Database**: MongoDB (Atlas).
*   **Storage**: Cloudinary / AWS S3 (Media).
*   **Payments**: Razorpay / Stripe.
*   **Maps**: Google Maps Platform.

### Performance & UX
*   **Real-time Sync**: Dashboard updates reflect instantly in the app.
*   **Optimistic UI**: Smooth transitions and skeleton loaders.
*   **SEO Optimized**: Semantic HTML and meta tags for web portals.
*   **Mobile First**: Responsive layouts tailored for all device sizes.

---

## 4. UPCOMING ROADMAP (The "Perfect" Flow)
1.  **[PHASE 1]** Refine Owner Tools & Design Gallery (DONE)
2.  **[PHASE 2]** Customer Authentication (Mobile OTP)
3.  **[PHASE 3]** Digital Measurement System Implementation
4.  **[PHASE 4]** Real-time Order Tracking (Pipeline UI)
5.  **[PHASE 5]** Payment Integration & Payout Logic
6.  **[PHASE 6]** Google Maps Location & Distance Matrix

---

## 5. DETAILED NEXT STEPS (Phase 2 & 3)

### PHASE 2: CUSTOMER AUTHENTICATION (The "Zomato-style" Login)
*   **OTP Integration**: Implement a mobile number-based login flow.
    *   *Task*: Create a backend route `POST /api/auth/otp/send` and `verify`.
    *   *Task*: Integrate an SMS service (Twilio/Firebase Auth) for real OTPs.
*   **Customer Profile**: A dedicated database collection for `Customers`.
    *   *Fields*: Name, Mobile, Saved Addresses, Order History, Favorites.
*   **Session Management**: JWT (JSON Web Token) with long expiration for mobile persistence.

### PHASE 3: DIGITAL MEASUREMENT SYSTEM (The "Virtual Tailor")
*   **Measurement Categories**: Create profiles for different outfit types.
    *   *Blouse*: Bust, Waist, Shoulders, Sleeve Length, Front Neck, Back Neck.
    *   *Lehenga/Saree*: Waist, Hip, Length, Inseam.
*   **UI/UX**:
    *   *Visual Guide*: Add small "Help Icons" with images showing how to take each measurement.
    *   *Multiple Profiles*: Allow users to save measurements for "Self", "Daughter", "Friend", etc.
*   **Integration**: Automatically attach the selected Measurement Profile when a customer places an order.
*   **AI Integration (Future)**: Use camera/AI to suggest measurements (Advanced).

---

## 6. PERFECT UI DESIGN SYSTEM (The Zomato Standard)

To achieve a "Zomato-level" premium feel, the app must follow these UI/UX principles:

### A. VISUAL AESTHETICS
*   **Color Palette**: 
    *   *Primary*: Deep Maroon/Burgundy (`#8B0000`) for elegance and luxury.
    *   *Accent*: Soft Gold (`#C89B3C`) for premium highlights.
    *   *Background*: Off-White/Cream (`#FAF6F2`) instead of plain white for a "boutique" feel.
*   **Typography**: Use **Inter** or **Outfit** fonts. Bold headers for clarity and medium weights for readability.
*   **Glassmorphism**: Use subtle blur effects on headers and floating buttons to create depth.

### B. THE "ZOMATO" COMPONENTS
*   **Smart Search Bar**: Sticky at the top with auto-suggestions and recent searches.
*   **Skeleton Loaders**: Instead of loading spinners, show gray shapes that match the content layout while data is fetching.
*   **Micro-Animations**:
    *   *Smooth Transitions*: Use `framer-motion` for shared element transitions when moving from list to details.
    *   *Haptic Feedback*: Subtle vibrations on mobile when a user "Hearts" a design.
*   **Floating Action Buttons (FAB)**: A "Call Now" or "Book Appointment" button that stays visible while scrolling.

### C. THE "PERFECT" BOUTIQUE CARD
*   **Aspect Ratio**: 4:5 for boutique covers (vertical looks better for fashion).
*   **Dynamic Chips**: Overlay badges like "Verified", "Top Rated", or "Fast Delivery".
*   **Gradient Overlays**: Dark gradient at the bottom of images to make white text readable.

### D. INTERACTION FLOW (The "Joy" Factor)
*   **Infinite Scroll**: Smoothly loading more boutiques as the user scrolls down.
*   **Pull-to-Refresh**: Custom "VS Boutique" icon animation when refreshing the list.
*   **Interactive Maps**: Users can drag a pin to set their precise delivery location.

---

## 7. FLOW ARCHITECTURE (User vs. Owner)

### A. CUSTOMER APP FLOW (The Shopping Journey)
```text
HOME SCREEN (Nearby Boutiques)
 ├── Search & Category Filters
 └── Boutique Card (Click)
      └── BOUTIQUE DETAILS (About Tab)
           ├── Our Specialties (Icons)
           ├── Popular Designs (Carousel)
           └── Book Appointment (CTA)
      └── DESIGNS TAB (Full Gallery)
           └── Design Detail (Click)
                └── ADD TO CART / ORDER NOW
                     └── SELECT MEASUREMENT PROFILE
                          ├── Use Existing (Self/Family)
                          └── Add New (Digital Tape)
                               └── PAYMENT GATEWAY (Razorpay/Stripe)
                                    └── ORDER CONFIRMED
                                         └── LIVE TRACKING (Pipeline)
                                              └── RATE & REVIEW (Post-Delivery)
```

### B. OWNER DASHBOARD FLOW (The Business Manager)
```text
OWNER LOGIN
 ├── DASHBOARD (Stats: Sales, Orders, New Clients)
 ├── BOUTIQUE PROFILE (Live Simulator Sync)
 │    ├── Edit Identity (Logo, Cover, Description)
 │    └── Edit Services (Specialty Tags)
 ├── DESIGN GALLERY (The Showcase)
 │    ├── Add New Design (Photo, Price, Category)
 │    └── Manage Availability (In-Stock/Out-of-Stock)
 ├── ORDER MANAGEMENT (The Kitchen/Workshop)
 │    ├── NEW ORDERS (Accept/Reject)
 │    ├── ACTIVE ORDERS (Update Status: Cutting -> Stitching -> Ready)
 │    └── COMPLETED ORDERS (History & Payments)
 └── ANALYTICS & PAYOUTS
      ├── Monthly Revenue
      └── Request Payout from Admin
```



